        "label": "Lay out a calendar view",
        "status": "active",
        "job": "Arrange time blocks for a day, week, month or agenda view, split overlapping blocks into columns, and name the blocks that clash",
        "description": "Takes time blocks and the views the person keeps (each a record naming a geometry: a time grid with a number of day columns, a month grid, or an agenda list, and the numbers it reads) and gives back the days to show with the blocks on each. In a time grid, blocks that overlap in time share the day column in equal parts, and every set of blocks that overlap is listed as a clash. Days are the person's own: give utc_offset_minutes and every time moves by it before it is cut into a day; an all-day block is a date and is not moved. There is no clock: the day comes from the anchor, the selected block, the first block or the range start. A view whose geometry is not known is answered with a notice.",
        "input_schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": ["blocks", "views"],
